# Copy to .env (gitignored). NEVER commit real values.
#
# In TrueForge local mode, the model provider API key is configured in TrueForge's own UI,
# not here. This file documents any env the arena / MCP server may need.

# Arena subnet — must match arena/docker-compose.yml AND
# mcp-server/src/policy/networkPolicy.ts (ARENA_CIDRS_V4).
CRUCIBLE_ARENA_SUBNET=10.42.0.0/24

# Port the Crucible MCP server listens on (adjust to your setup).
CRUCIBLE_MCP_PORT=8848

# Agent-facing artifact root served by the fetch_file MCP tool. Files under
# <root>/<challengeId>/ are readable; this is deliberately SEPARATE from the arena container
# sources so a target's solution/flag is never served through the tool. Defaults to
# mcp-server/challenge-files/ when unset.
# CRUCIBLE_CHALLENGE_FILES_ROOT=./mcp-server/challenge-files

# --- MCP HTTP endpoint auth (used by arena/docker-compose.yml + scripts/trueforge-setup.mjs) ---
# Shared secret so only TrueForge (which sends the header) can invoke the MCP tools. Generate a
# random value, e.g.  export CRUCIBLE_MCP_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
# CRUCIBLE_MCP_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_HEX

# --- TrueForge wiring (scripts/trueforge-setup.mjs) — all have safe local defaults ---
# TRUEFORGE_URL=http://localhost:8790        # must be loopback
# MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8848/mcp          # the containerized MCP server; must be loopback
# MODEL_PROVIDER=openai                       # native: openai|anthropic|google-gemini|fireworks|
#                                             # zai|moonshot|alibaba|together — OR any name when
#                                             # MODEL_BASE_URL is set (OpenAI-compatible, see below)
# MODEL_ID=gpt-5.5                            # upstream model id sent to the provider
# MODEL_NAME=gpt-5-5                          # local name (a-z0-9-); the agent uses <PROVIDER>/<MODEL_NAME>
# CRUCIBLE_ENABLE_SANDBOX=false               # agent sandbox off by default (egress not constrained
#                                             # in standalone mode — see docs/SECURITY_MODEL.md §3a)
# CRUCIBLE_AUDIT_LOG=/tmp/crucible-audit.jsonl # OPTIONAL: set on the MCP server to append a JSONL
#                                             # gated-action audit log (connect/http_request + policy
#                                             # decision + outcome). Path must be writable by the MCP
#                                             # server. Unset = disabled. See docs/EVIDENCE.md. Non-secret.
#
# OpenAI-compatible providers (e.g. Groq) aren't native — set MODEL_BASE_URL to register them as a
# `custom` provider. Example (Groq): NOTE free tier is ~8000 tokens/min and this agent's request is
# larger, so use Groq's Dev tier or a provider with adequate limits.
# MODEL_PROVIDER=groq
# MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1   # must be https (external cloud API; validated)
# MODEL_ID=openai/gpt-oss-120b                # a model your key can access (GET .../v1/models)
# MODEL_NAME=gpt-oss-120b                     # agent uses groq/gpt-oss-120b
# TF_MODEL_API_KEY should then be your GROQ_API_KEY.

# Do NOT put a real model key in the repo. Supply it via the environment at run time only:
# TF_MODEL_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE_ME              # provider API key — NEVER commit a real value
